{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1067650-world-of-darkness-b-team","id":1067650,"title":"World of Darkness B Team","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-03-24T09:39:07-07:00","id":1067650,"title":"World of Darkness B Team","content":"I was thinking of running a classic World of Darkness game that didn't allow any of the creature types with their own dedicated hard bound core rulebook. Creatures with character generation described in those books would be allowed so long as they weren't the primary featured creature type of that book as would creatures with character generation in soft bound splats or elsewhere.<br /> <br /> This means (unless I am mistaken) things like ghouls and revenants would be okay as would Sorcerers, Demon Hunters (as per Demon Hunter X), and even creatures from the bygone bestiary.<br /> <br /> What are the other things that could be played under these constraints and where do I find the char gen for them? I'm sure I'm missing a lot of stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T11:44:56-07:00","id":1067716,"title":"","content":"Let's see...if I'm not mistaken..<br /> <br /> Kin, Sorcerors, Psychics, Ghouls, Acolytes, Bygones, Fomori, Dhampirs, Spirits, Arcanists, Seafolk, Mafiosis, the dreaded 'Gypsies', Government agents (Project Twilight), Demon Hunters, Enchanted (Changeling companions), Damned (Demon companions).<br /> <br /> If one wants, they COULD include Inanimae (Changeling), Hsien (changeling, Land of Eight Million Dreams) and Earthbound (Demon) to the list..although the last one in particular is not Player Material, and the first two are pretty much just derivatives of Kithain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T12:01:46-07:00","id":1067721,"title":"","content":"Fomori have character generation rules? Gypsies... I forgot about those.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T12:06:24-07:00","id":1067723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacecat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1067650-world-of-darkness-b-team?p=1067721#post1067721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fomori have character generation rules? Gypsies... I forgot about those.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. Freak Legion and Possessed both feature rules for making Fomori. Rules for Kami, Drones, and Gorgons can be found in the latter, also.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T12:49:57-07:00","id":1067745,"title":"","content":"Actually, what books would I need for the complete set of playable thingies?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T13:06:19-07:00","id":1067752,"title":"","content":"V20 has character creation rules for ghouls and revenants<br /> Sorceror has character creation rules for various hedge magicians<br /> Bygone Bestiary is for Bygones and other such creatures<br /> Freak Legion is for Fomori<br /> Possessed for Fomori, Kami, Drones, and Gorgons (I don't even know what Kami, Drones, and Gorgons are exactly)<br /> Demon Hunter X for Shih &amp; Strike force Demon Hunters<br /> Enchanted for Changeling companions (I don't even know what these are exactly)<br /> Damned for Demon companions (I don't even know what these are exactly)<br /> Gypsy (Why not. I doubt anyone will play one)<br /> Kindred of the east is a soft splat right?<br /> Where are the Dhampirs character creation noted?<br /> Land of Eight Million Dreams for Hsien<br /> <br /> What are inanimae?<br /> Spirits have a proper character creation ruleset?<br /> Arcanists?<br /> Seafolk?<br /> Mafiosis?<br /> Government agents (Project Twilight)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12480,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","user":"Spacecat","date":".  typo correction 03-24-2017, 07:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T15:12:27-07:00","id":1067806,"title":"","content":"Inanimae and Seafolk are things from Changeling. Inanimae are detailed in Inanimae: the Secret Way. Seafolk are in WOD: Blood-Dimmed Tides.<br /> <br /> Spirits have enough rules to play them, though I can't think of any book that actually has &quot;starting creation&quot; rules. There's a few places for rules for mortals stuck in the Umbra too long becoming spirits though.<br /> <br /> Arcanists are members of the Arcanum, a Mage based organization of academics and investigators that seek out the supernatural. They're in the Halls of the Arcanum (though referenced in other places, and most members are just mortals with potential access to supernatural assets).<br /> <br /> WOD: Mafia has a general mortal creation rules, and discusses playing members of organized crime in general.<br /> <br /> There's a few government agencies in the books over the years. Hunters Hunted or Hunters Hunted II, Project Twilight, etc.<br /> <br /> There's also some snags in the way this is phrased. For example, where are mummies and Kuei-jin in this? Neither was ever given a true core book. But as supplemental groups. Though both received hardcover books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T15:23:34-07:00","id":1067813,"title":"","content":"Blood Dimmed Tides for seafaring creatures of various forms.<br /> <br /> KotE was a hardcover supplement for VtM, as was Mummy<br /> <br /> Various 'Year of the Hunter' books were the same character generation (mortal) with new groups to be members of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T15:44:39-07:00","id":1067822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacecat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1067650-world-of-darkness-b-team?p=1067752#post1067752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Possessed for Fomori, Kami, Drones, and Gorgons (I don't even know what Kami, Drones, and Gorgons are exactly)<br /> ...<br /> Enchanted for Changeling companions (I don't even know what these are exactly)<br /> ...<br /> Gypsy (Why not. I doubt anyone will pay one)<br /> ...<br /> Where are the Dhampirs character creation noted?<br /> <br /> <br /> What are inanimae?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Drones and Gorgons are to Fomori what the Weaver and the Wyld are to the Wyrm, respectively. Kami are the (usually, sometimes) Gaian equivalent. <br /> <br /> Enchanted covered a few things, the one I mainly remember being mortals born with blood relations to Changelings, sometimes giving them access to Kith birthrights or frailties as well as some other abilities. <br /> <br /> Gypsies are just people. Anything covered in WoD: Gypsy can be done (often better) with the stuff in Sorcerer and other books. (The exception is the knife fighting power which IIRC was just an adaption of the rules for Celerity; at one point many years ago, ideas were tossed around of a Sorcery &quot;path of war&quot; or something, that would let you make extra attacks and other effects, for use by unAwakened members of the Akashic Brotherhood, Syndicate agents trained in Gun-Kata and so on.)<br /> <br /> Inanimae are a subset of fey tied to the elements and dwelling within inanimate objects (rocks, trees, puppets, etc.). It has one of my favorite Changeling character templates ever, the Baseball Mavin, who is a baseball bat. (I'm pretty sure it was inspired by Wraith/Vampire: The Dark Ages developer Richard Dansky, who is a huge baseball fan.)<br /> <br /> I believe there is a KotE book called Dampyrs. There are also some bits on western dampirs in Time of Thin Blood, I think. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T16:24:40-07:00","id":1067836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1067650-world-of-darkness-b-team?p=1067806#post1067806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's also some snags in the way this is phrased. For example, where are mummies and Kuei-jin in this? Neither was ever given a true core book. But as supplemental groups. Though both received hardcover books.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, this game idea isn't exactly a product of deep thinking and the delineation is rather arbitrary.<br /> What do you mean by not being given a true core book though?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T17:19:15-07:00","id":1067850,"title":"","content":"Aren't the Damned just Thralls? Or are they something else?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T18:08:47-07:00","id":1067873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1067650-world-of-darkness-b-team?p=1067822#post1067822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It has one of my favorite Changeling character templates ever, the Baseball Mavin, who is a baseball bat. (I'm pretty sure it was inspired by Wraith/Vampire: The Dark Ages developer Richard Dansky, who is a huge baseball fan.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I never heard about this! As a huge baseball fan, I've got to check this out now. Doh'!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T20:02:53-07:00","id":1067896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacecat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1067650-world-of-darkness-b-team?p=1067836#post1067836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you mean by not being given a true core book though?</div> </div> </div> </div>All three editions of Mummy (the first two are softcover supplements, the third is the one that's hardcover and a bit more &quot;full game&quot; in presentation), and KotE all require other books for the core rules. They lack full rules on common traits like Attributes, Abilities, Willpower, etc. and don't contain the dice rolling rules or similar features. They're as &quot;incomplete&quot; as something like Sorcerer (the 1e/2e Mummy books are very comparable to WOD: Sorcerer), even if they contain much more information because they cover full supernatural societies instead of detailing things that are secondary to other things.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T20:13:23-07:00","id":1067900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1067650-world-of-darkness-b-team?p=1067822#post1067822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Drones and Gorgons are to Fomori what the Weaver and the Wyld are to the Wyrm, respectively. Kami are the (usually, sometimes) Gaian equivalent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1067650-world-of-darkness-b-team?p=1067822#post1067822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gypsies are just people. Anything covered in WoD: Gypsy can be done (often better) with the stuff in Sorcerer and other books.</div> </div> </div> </div>The fact that this title was published amazes me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1067650-world-of-darkness-b-team?p=1067822#post1067822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Inanimae are a subset of fey tied to the elements and dwelling within inanimate objects (rocks, trees, puppets, etc.). It has one of my favorite Changeling character templates ever, the Baseball Mavin, who is a baseball bat. (I'm pretty sure it was inspired by Wraith/Vampire: The Dark Ages developer Richard Dansky, who is a huge baseball fan.)<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This is awesome.<br /> The sort of game I have in mind was something of a bizarre detective agency where all the players play these sorts of characters and solve supernatural mysteries while trying to keep alive, safe, and sane in a zany rendition of the classic WoD. I plan to give them an average of 3 cases at the same time. One would be a normal mundane, completely easy case (Like find the lost cat, get proof of a husband cheating on his wife, find this debtor); another would be a somewhat more difficult mundane case, like something from cold case or CSI whatever; and the remaining one would be the supernatural related case. Then sometimes I'd mix things up a bit, like have it so that maybe a vampire hired them to find his perfectly normal missing cat that is missing for mundane reasons, the debtor turns out to be a paranoid ex-military nutcase who will be as serious a threat to the party as your standard supernatural creature, and the other mundane case will be weirder than the supernatural one by far. At this point, it's all still in the conceptual stage.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T21:52:20-07:00","id":1067917,"title":"","content":"Hsien, Inanimae, and Mer are Changelings, so they overpower mortal characters pretty quick (as do Demons, KJ, and Mummies). If you want an action game, adapt Dhampyrs from KotE. They are much more powerful than any other form of beginning lesser supernatural (at least without selling their soul) and I often use a version of them as replacements for Western Dhampir and Revenants. The Shih are comparable to KotW Dhampyr, though you have to adapt the Chi rules from 2e to Revised, and they are more fragile.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T10:03:12-07:00","id":1068029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1067650-world-of-darkness-b-team?p=1067917#post1067917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hsien, Inanimae, and Mer are Changelings</div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=k5hWWe-ts2s\" data-code=\"k5hWWe-ts2s\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/k5hWWe-ts2s/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> , so they overpower mortal characters pretty quick (as do Demons, KJ, and Mummies). If you want an action game, adapt Dhampyrs from KotE. They are much more powerful than any other form of beginning lesser supernatural (at least without selling their soul) and I often use a version of them as replacements for Western Dhampir and Revenants. The Shih are comparable to KotW Dhampyr, though you have to adapt the Chi rules from 2e to Revised, and they are more fragile. </div> </div> </div>There are already Revised Chi rules, in the book on the Dhampyrs (short version - it's bashing damage and the mortal, Shih or not, gets a soak roll to avoid taking damage from Chi use). Also, Dhampyrs that develop their P'o shoot even further past other second-stringers, since it means that they can get even more dots in Black Wind, and they have more control over it than the Hungry Dead proper do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T10:56:07-07:00","id":1068044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1067650-world-of-darkness-b-team?p=1067896#post1067896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> All three editions of Mummy (the first two are softcover supplements, the third is the one that's hardcover and a bit more &quot;full game&quot; in presentation), and KotE all require other books for the core rules. They lack full rules on common traits like Attributes, Abilities, Willpower, etc. and don't contain the dice rolling rules or similar features. They're as &quot;incomplete&quot; as something like Sorcerer (the 1e/2e Mummy books are very comparable to WOD: Sorcerer), even if they contain much more information because they cover full supernatural societies instead of detailing things that are secondary to other things.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see. I don't plan to include them as possible player characters, mainly to dredge up the even more obscure creature types.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T10:59:20-07:00","id":1068047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1067650-world-of-darkness-b-team?p=1067917#post1067917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hsien, Inanimae, and Mer are Changelings, so they overpower mortal characters pretty quick (as do Demons, KJ, and Mummies). If you want an action game, adapt Dhampyrs from KotE. They are much more powerful than any other form of beginning lesser supernatural (at least without selling their soul) and I often use a version of them as replacements for Western Dhampir and Revenants. The Shih are comparable to KotW Dhampyr, though you have to adapt the Chi rules from 2e to Revised, and they are more fragile.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm more going for a comedy mystery vibe, not that power level is a huge concern. I'm used to handling all sorts of power levels and even mixed ones. I'm more interested in what weird ideas players will come up with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T11:10:01-07:00","id":1068052,"title":"","content":"Changing Breeds now confound me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T12:19:24-07:00","id":1068065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacecat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1067650-world-of-darkness-b-team?p=1068052#post1068052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Changing Breeds now confound me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is there anything in specific?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T17:29:12-07:00","id":1068129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacecat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1067650-world-of-darkness-b-team?p=1068052#post1068052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Changing Breeds now confound me.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're all more or less on par with werewolves, but with a handful of exceptions (the rare Corax that hangs around a Garou pack, the Asian Beast Courts, the African Ahadi), each breed usually does its own thing and doesn't really interact with others that much. You could do something with a Nuwusha, Kitsune, Corax and Bastet all hanging out together for a few months, or a Bastet working with an Orphan and a Risen, since PCs usually tend to be exceptions to these sort of things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T18:06:33-07:00","id":1068131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1067650-world-of-darkness-b-team?p=1068065#post1068065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is there anything in specific?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not very familiar with werewolf, so, technically speaking, under the restrictions I already mentioned, would they be allowed for play? I don't have access to the werewolf core rules at the moment. (Someone else in my group has it and i won't be meeting them for a week)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T18:32:36-07:00","id":1068136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1067650-world-of-darkness-b-team?p=1068129#post1068129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They're all more or less on par with werewolves, but with a handful of exceptions (the rare Corax that hangs around a Garou pack, the Asian Beast Courts, the African Ahadi), each breed usually does its own thing and doesn't really interact with others that much. You could do something with a Nuwusha, Kitsune, Corax and Bastet all hanging out together for a few months, or a Bastet working with an Orphan and a Risen, since PCs usually tend to be exceptions to these sort of things.</div> </div> </div> </div>My main concern is that I don't want too many players to gravitate to one or more creature type and I'm not familiar enough with werewolf and changing breeds to know exactly what that means with regards to them and if they are actually allowed or not allowed by what i have written.<br /> <br /> (Not a huge deal either way for me except I really don't know)<br /> <br /> I any case, until someone helps me out or I get to read the book thoroughly, I'll focus on making up some mysteries to solve for these guys. Suggestions are appreciated too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T18:40:41-07:00","id":1068140,"title":"","content":"Fera are very powerful, probably the most powerful beginning creatures in cWoD, so the Fera players would overshadow the non-Fera players. In addition, it is hard to threaten Fera characters without killing everything else off (unless you have every enemy inexplicably carrying silver weapons). Generally, I would suggest a Fera game or a non-Fera game, though you could have Kinfolk Sorcerers in a non-Fera game without any trouble if you wanted to have a reason for Fera NPCs to help out the group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T19:41:51-07:00","id":1068148,"title":"","content":"To further emphasize Aya Tari's point, keep in mind that Mokole can become building-sized kaiju monsters far larger than the beasts of prehistory that they can recall, and Gurahl can heal one of the biggest issues in the cosmos (the Wyrm's madness), if given enough Gnosis and uninterrupted access to the center of Malfeas. You know, in addition to being able to turn into a 20-foot tall bear monster that can Rage-boost Strength to 20.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T19:46:44-07:00","id":1068149,"title":"","content":"So by my original rules, do you expect most players to gravitate towards changing breeds?<br /> <br /> So, if I limited the game to creatures with character creation rules, but not any of the creature types with their own dedicated hard bound core rulebook specifically for their creature type and no Fera, would that leave anything else that might be too much of a player magnet or just too overpowered?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T20:00:55-07:00","id":1068153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacecat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1067650-world-of-darkness-b-team?p=1068149#post1068149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So by my original rules, do you expect most players to gravitate towards changing breeds?<br /> <br /> So, if I limited the game to creatures with character creation rules, but not any of the creature types with their own dedicated hard bound core rulebook specifically for their creature type and no Fera, would that leave anything else that might be too much of a player magnet or just too overpowered?</div> </div> </div> </div>Put more simply, Fera aren't B-team monsters. They are on par with Garou, at the very least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T20:14:36-07:00","id":1068157,"title":"","content":"Ok. Thanks. So no Fera then. Anything else I should be worried about?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T10:40:30-07:00","id":1068338,"title":"","content":"I would avoid Demons, Hsien, Inanimae, Mer, Reborn, and Risen because they will also be power magnets for various reasons. Your best bets would be Dhampyr (from KotE), Shih, Sorcerers (created with the Equality of All rules, with characters being allowed to be Ghouls, Kinain, or Kinfolk by taking the appropriate Merits).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T13:45:02-07:00","id":1068403,"title":"","content":"I think an across-the-board ruling that one must be some sort of human at the core, rather than a hybrid, reanimated corpse, possessing spirit, etc. will help keep the power level down to a manageable setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T15:59:52-07:00","id":1068452,"title":"","content":"IIRC, the &quot;B-list&quot; (or as I refer to them, Twilight People, since they exist on the edges of the various subcultures of Darkness like the Kindred, Garou, etc.) are:<br /> <br /> Ghouls and Revenants (I really wish they'd been called something else, since the term refers to walking corpses)<br /> Kinfolk (whose main deal is just that they don't go into a mindless panic state when seeing werebeasts in full combat mode, but can end up with special powers sometimes)<br /> Sorcerers<br /> Mediums<br /> Kinain (the fey equivalent of Kinfolk)<br /> Witchhunters (the people covered in Hunters Hunted, The Inquisition, Project: Twilight, Halls of the Arcanum)<br /> Psychics (whom I wish had had their own book instead of being stuffed into Sorcerer Revised)<br /> Shaman (who are covered - kind of badly IMO - in the Spirit Ways and - much better - Dreamspeakers Revised)<br /> Criminals (the Mafia, as well as some stuff covered in the KotE book Killing Streets)<br /> Strike Force Zero and The Shih (Demon Hunter X)<br /> <br /> Things like Mummies, Changing Breeds, The Risen, Inanimae, the various Asian supernaturals, Demons, and Hunters/Imbued are full blown Creatures of Darkness (A-List)<br /> <br /> IIRC, the various forms of Possessed sort of fluctuate somewhere between the two depending on how powerful (and inhuman) they are. <br /> <br /> There are also Bystanders, failed Hunters/Imbued who don't get any powers, but I can't recall if there is anything that actually differentiates them from normal people other than being made aware that supernatural monsters exist. (I think they're in the Hunter Players Guide)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T16:29:03-07:00","id":1068464,"title":"","content":"I appreciate the suggestions. Maybe I should just make a complete A-List listand say: You can't play this!!!<br /> <br /> Where do Demon Companions (someone mentioned them I think) fit in this?<br /> What are the mer like exactly? (I have no picture of them nor access to the books at the moment)<br /> What are the Reborn? I'm sure I read of them some time ago. <br /> <br /> I do still want to fit in bygones and inanimae, despite recommendations.<br /> PC bygones are somewhat limited anyway by 7/5/3 in Attributes, 11/7/4 in Abilities and 6 points worth of powers. Though they do have 21 freebies, the weirder creatures will have other problems with regards to being part of a detective agency.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T17:12:20-07:00","id":1068482,"title":"","content":"It's been so long since I've looked at my copy of Demon that I can't recall anything about Companions, unfortunately. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I <i>think</i> the term for them are Thralls and they are in the book Damned &amp; Deceived. <br /> <br /> The Mer were in World of Darkness: Blood-Dimmed Tides and, IIRC, came in two types: the &quot;Seelie-like&quot; Merfolk fish ones (mermaids and the like) and the &quot;Unseelie-like&quot; Merdhuacha invertebrate ones (squids, crabs, etc.).<br /> <br /> IIRC, Reborn is another name for Mummies. <br /> <br /> I was always a little disappointed that Bygone Bestiary was a historical book, given all the weird modern urban legend stuff you can do with in in the modern World of Darkness. Experimental androids who gained sentience and wandered off, Japanese slit-mouthed women, black-eyed children, Slenderman, the chupacabra, boo hags/night witches, the letiche, Batboy, the Red Dwarf of Detroit, the Monkey Man of Delhi, Greys and so on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T02:00:11-07:00","id":1068583,"title":"","content":"Thralls can get a variety of bonuses from the Pacts they make; from extra dots in Attributes and Abilities, more Willpower (all of those are bought with Freebie Points, per 1 point of Faith the Thrall has 10 Freebie Points spent on them), weaker versions of the Lores that the Demons have and a variety of utility powers (immunity to mind control, immunity to possession and so on). But Thralls are rarely of enough Faith to have a lot of abilities: two dots is the norm, three for faithful, four for zealous and five for Pope-level faith. So finding a fitting Thrall with four dots is a feat in and of itself. This severely limits how powerful a Thrall can be.<br /> <br /> This would make them a bit more powerful than something like a Ghoul, but less powerful than, say, a Sorcerer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T03:44:30-07:00","id":1068600,"title":"","content":"What's out so far: Vampires, Mages, Werewolves and Changing Breeds, Mummies, Demons, Kuei Jin...<br /> <br /> on that note, how powerful are changeling on the scale of things? I've never had them in a non-changeling game.<br /> <br /> And for that matter, wraiths... how would wraiths even fit in?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12480,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","user":"Spacecat","date":". 03-27-2017, 06:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T04:27:32-07:00","id":1068606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1067650-world-of-darkness-b-team?p=1068482#post1068482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was always a little disappointed that Bygone Bestiary was a historical book, given all the weird modern urban legend stuff you can do with in in the modern World of Darkness. Experimental androids who gained sentience and wandered off, Japanese slit-mouthed women, black-eyed children, Slenderman, the chupacabra, boo hags/night witches, the letiche, Batboy, the Red Dwarf of Detroit, the Monkey Man of Delhi, Greys and so on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, that would be amazing. Modern 'Bygones' (Which are not quite bygone, now are they?) being the urban legends and spoopy modern legends.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T07:29:13-07:00","id":1068658,"title":"","content":"I think modern bygones deserve their own book and, yes, bygones might not be a good name for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T08:08:46-07:00","id":1068675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacecat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1067650-world-of-darkness-b-team?p=1068600#post1068600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's out so far: Vampires, Mages, Werewolves and Changing Breeds, Mummies, Demons, Kuei Jin...<br /> <br /> on that note, how powerful are changeling on the scale of things? I've never had them in a non-changeling game.</div> </div> </div> </div>High enough to contend with the other monsters. C20 might push the bar further, seeing as how they're getting a form of Unleashing for their Arts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And for that matter, wraiths... how would wraiths even fit in? </div> </div> </div>Moliation. Oh, you meant on a power scale? Some of their stuff can get pretty obscene, like Tempus Fugit and its time-alteration effects. Arcanoi tend to be pretty powerful, in general, though some have rather specialized uses (Castigation is for controlling Shadows, which is useful to Wraiths but not something that others might see as having an overt effect until it isn't there to keep a ghost's bad half from taking over).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T11:09:16-07:00","id":1068759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacecat</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> And for that matter, wraiths... how would wraiths even fit in?<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1067650-world-of-darkness-b-team?p=1068675#post1068675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Moliation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I giggled.<br /> <br /> On another note, I was thinking a phoenix or dragon is going to be stronger than a ghoul. If balance is a concern, bygones might be a bit<i> too beastly</i> for the B team.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T11:55:34-07:00","id":1068782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1067650-world-of-darkness-b-team?p=1068759#post1068759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I giggled.<br /> <br /> On another note, I was thinking a phoenix or dragon is going to be stronger than a ghoul. If balance is a concern, bygones might be a bit<i> too beastly</i> for the B team.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, I can't even reach the lowest Drake stats using bygone PC character creation rules. Just getting the Attributes would cost 30 freebie points, never mind their powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T11:58:30-07:00","id":1068783,"title":"","content":"So currently, no Vampires, Mages, Werewolves and Changing Breeds, Mummies, Demons, Kuei Jin, Wraiths, or Changelings.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T13:24:58-07:00","id":1068830,"title":"","content":"It sounds like you're going for a Year of the Ally type of game \u2014 <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Year_of_the_Ally\" target=\"_blank\">http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Year_of_the_Ally</a><br /> <br /> They're the mortal or nearly mortal allies of the core book supernatural creatures. Here are their names followed by their game line and the primary books with information about them:<ul><li>Ghouls (Vampire: The Masquerade) \u2014 Ghouls: Fatal Addiction, V20, Ghouls and Revenants</li> <li>Kinfolk (Werewolf: The Apocalypse) \u2014 Kinfolk: The Unsung Heroes, W20, Kinfolk: A Breed Apart</li> <li>Custos (Mage: The Ascension) \u2014 Ascension's Right Hand</li> <li>Mediums (Wraith: The Oblivion) \u2014 Mediums: Speakers with the Dead</li> <li>Kinain (Changeling: The Dreaming) \u2014 The Enchanted, C20</li> <li>Bystanders (Hunter: The Reckoning) \u2014 Hunter Players Guide</li> <li>Thralls (Demon: The Fallen) \u2014 Damned and Decieved</li> </ul>Sorcerers are mortal practitioners of hedge magic. They were originally a stand alone group not tied to any particular game. Their book was a black cover World of Darkness book. The revised version of their book tried to put them under the Mage umbrella, but it was an awkward fit. M20 seems to be reversing course on that.<br /> <br /> Edit to add: I completely forgot about the W20 kinfolk book. For some reason I was thinking it wasn't out yet, but there it is, sitting on my bookshelf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":648,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","user":"PookaKnight","date":". 03-29-2017, 09:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T14:27:58-07:00","id":1068878,"title":"","content":"Not exactly that but almost that. Thanks. Something like the same idea from the opposite perspective but that list really does help. .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T17:03:05-07:00","id":1068940,"title":"","content":"Bystanders probably aren't worth including without the Imbued around. They have extremely little above normal humans, and most of that is to make them useful psychological and emotional support for the Imbued. Of course, the Imbued themselves aren't that powerful in the first place.<br /> <br /> It's also very hard to do much with Custos without using something else (like Sorcerer Revised) to model their abilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T18:44:18-07:00","id":1068971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1067650-world-of-darkness-b-team?p=1068940#post1068940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bystanders probably aren't worth including without the Imbued around. They have extremely little above normal humans, and most of that is to make them useful psychological and emotional support for the Imbued. Of course, the Imbued themselves aren't that powerful in the first place.<br /> <br /> It's also very hard to do much with Custos without using something else (like Sorcerer Revised) to model their abilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ascension's Right Hand has a fairly exhaustive list of general powers and capabilities. You could also model some of their capabilities with material from Demon Hunter X.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T22:27:18-07:00","id":1069114,"title":"","content":"A while back a buddy and I worked on an alternative setting where all vampires were eliminated hundreds of years ago and basically the only remnant of the them were Revenant families, who formed the basis of our new game, complete with factions composed of different families along with alternative politics and history. It was pretty interesting but I haven't had the chance to do anything with it. <br /> <br /> I also thought it would be interesting to match that setting with one where Garou likewise died out but the kinfolk remain and form the basis of their own game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T04:39:04-07:00","id":1069246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1067650-world-of-darkness-b-team?p=1068971#post1068971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ascension's Right Hand has a fairly exhaustive list of general powers and capabilities. You could also model some of their capabilities with material from Demon Hunter X.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering how much of that are the Numina (aka Hedge Magic, Psychic Powers, and True Faith) I'm not sure that's saying much. Forged by Dragon's Fire + Sorcerer's Revised + Mage Revised Merits and Flaws pretty covers even more ground than Ascension's Right Hand does.<br /> <br /> Though I'm frequently confused by the people that say Sorcerer Revised doesn't make sense as a mage focused book when Ascension's Right Hand has a chapter titled Numina.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T07:12:43-07:00","id":1069318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacecat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1067650-world-of-darkness-b-team?p=1068878#post1068878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not exactly that but almost that. Thanks. Something like the same idea from the opposite perspective but that list really does help. .</div> </div> </div> </div>So for mortals and nearly mortals who aren't allies of the supernaturals, there are the Year of the Hunter type books \u2014 <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Year_of_the_Hunter\" target=\"_blank\">http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Year_of_the_Hunter</a><br /> <br /> These guys tend to have fewer clear cut labels than the Year of the Ally counterparts. Also, since they're meant as antagonists, they're a bit more powerful than the allies. They're also hard to describe as evenly as the allies. For this list, it'll be game line, followed by the relevant books, and then a brief description of the subject matter.<ul><li>Vampire: The Masquerade \u2014 Hunters Hunted, The Inquisition, Hunters Hunted II<br /> Hunters Hunted focuses on lone mortal hunters. The Inquisition is about the Inquisition, better known as the Society of Leopold. Hunters Hunted II revisits lone mortal hunters plus most of the other Year of the Hunter groups.</li> <li>Werewolf: The Apocalypse \u2014 Project Twilight, (maybe Freak Legion, Possessed, and Subsidiaries: A Guide to Pentex)<br /> Project Twilights covers government organizations dealing with the supernatural.<br /> I mention Freak Legion, Possessed, and Subsidiaries because they technically meet your criteria, but they may be too supernatural for what you're after. Freak Legion and Possessed deal with mortals possessed by spirits. Subsidiaries is a book about Pentex, a supernaturally evil mega-corporation.</li> <li>Mage: The Ascension \u2014 Halls of the Arcanum<br /> The Arcanum is a group of mortals dedicated to studying the supernatural, think the Watchers from Buffy or Highlander.</li> <li>Wraith: The Oblivion \u2014 The Quick and the Dead<br /> Ghost hunters, both scientific and supernatural.</li> <li>Changeling: The Dreaming \u2014 The Autumn People, C20<br /> Covers both Autumn People and Dauntain. Autumn People are mortals so entrenched in their mundanity, magic fails around them. Dauntain are probably too supernatural. They're Changelings broken by Banality. C20 is giving them both a major overhaul.</li> <li>Hunter: The Reckoning \u2014 First Contact<br /> Describes most of the above from an Imbued perspective.</li> <li>Demon: The Fallen \u2014 Saviors and Destroyers<br /> Covers people of faith and mortal demon hunters.</li> <li>General World of Darkness \u2014 Sorcerer, Demon Hunter X, Mafia, Gypsies<br /> Of these, Mafia is probably closest to what you're looking for, mortal members of the Mafia who may or may not have a supernatural edge.<br /> As mentioned before, Sorcerer covers mortal hedge magic. Demon Hunter X covers the Shih and Strike Force Zero, two Asian anti-supernatural groups.<br /> Gypsies is mentioned only for completeness. It's super racist and should probably be ignored.</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":648,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","user":"PookaKnight","date":". 03-28-2017, 10:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T07:16:09-07:00","id":1069321,"title":"","content":"Further caveat: Pentex is actually pretty banally evil from day to day, rather than supernaturally evil. It does hire monsters for being monsters, but only for certain jobs and only in certain subsidiaries. King Distillaries is going to have far, far fewer fomori than Endron, which is lousy with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T12:01:12-07:00","id":1069521,"title":"","content":"To PookaKnight,<br /> <br /> Many many thanks.<br /> <br /> Just to clarify, my main concern is not so much to exclude certain groups because of their level of power but to exclude crowd favorites so that players will choose from among the more rarely used and the least used creature types. This incidentally seems to leave us with the weaker creature types. The power level of a creature type becomes a concern only in that creatures with significantly more power will become magnets for players and the last thing i want is for all the players in the entire group to pick the same creature type. It's okay for some creature types to be a bit stronger than others so long as it's not enough of a thing that more than half of the players will decide to play one. This is very relative criteria, of course, but it's the intent.<br /> <br /> That said, your lists have been a tremendous help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T13:21:05-07:00","id":1069578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1067650-world-of-darkness-b-team?p=1069318#post1069318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gypsies is mentioned only for completeness. It's super racist and should probably be ignored.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not so much racist as just super dumb and having little or nothing to do with the titular subject matter, either in the real world or in the context of the gothic horror genre (Stoker's Dracula or it's various movie adaptions, Doyle's The Adventure of the Speckled Band, Lovecraft's The Cats of Ulthar, DeLint's Mulengro, The Wolf Man, House of Frankenstein). A book that actually covered that, and talked about how various supernatural creatures can or can not fit into said cultures (vampires being both dead and needing to drink blood, or that werewolves, being shape shifters who are supernaturally seductive come across as stereotypical mullo, make it impossible for them to be part of a community), and how you can do actual Romani rites or beliefs with Path Magic or Psychic abilities, or do the stereotypical cinematic powers using Disciplines, Spheres, Arts, etc. for vampires, changelings or mages who want to go that route, would've been far more interesting. Instead, all we got was a what looked like someone's first draft of a cheesy early 80s fantasy novel mixed with some of the laziest attempts at faction creation ever. (Honestly, of the five &quot;families of power&quot; we get one with the same name as a vampire clan, one with the same name vampires use for werewolves, and one with the Romani name for grandmother.) Blah, I say. Blah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":12890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","user":"No One of Consequence","date":". 03-28-2017, 04:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T16:15:22-07:00","id":1069693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1067650-world-of-darkness-b-team?p=1069578#post1069578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not so much racist as just super dumb</div> </div> </div> </div>Both, really. Racist crap tends to come from being, at best, super lazy about handling of material.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and having little or nothing to do with the titular subject matter, either in the real world or in the context of the gothic horror genre (Stoker's Dracula or it's various movie adaptions, Doyle's The Adventure of the Speckled Band, Lovecraft's The Cats of Ulthar, DeLint's Mulengro, The Wolf Man, House of Frankenstein). A book that actually covered that, and talked about how various supernatural creatures can or can not fit into said cultures (vampires being both dead and needing to drink blood, or that werewolves, being shape shifters who are supernaturally seductive come across as stereotypical mullo, make it impossible for them to be part of a community), and how you can do actual Romani rites or beliefs with Path Magic or Psychic abilities, or do the stereotypical cinematic powers using Disciplines, Spheres, Arts, etc. for vampires, changelings or mages who want to go that route, would've been far more interesting. Instead, all we got was a what looked like someone's first draft of a cheesy early 80s fantasy novel mixed with some of the laziest attempts at faction creation ever. (Honestly, of the five &quot;families of power&quot; we get one with the same name as a vampire clan, one with the same name vampires use for werewolves, and one with the Romani name for grandmother.) Blah, I say. Blah. </div> </div> </div>Silent Striders Revised had commentary about this, and why they don't have good ties with Rroma (if any werewolves could be said to have ever had good ties with any group of humans). It also mentions what you just did as coming across like a slap in the face to Garou who are born among the Rroma and end up being considered to be vampires or something about the same. Talk about something to trigger Rage rolls...<br /> <br /> However, a specific book dedicated to a specific ethnic origin and any hypothetical interactions with various monsters in the WoD would still be intensely weird. There are probably other books - splats, location books, etc. - that could provide a better place with a tighter thesis for why it's there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T20:37:35-07:00","id":1069832,"title":"","content":"Regardless, I doubt that anyone are going to use the Romani, so their book can be ignored because it only effects 0.1% of humanity. The much more insulting book was Kindred of the Ebony Kingdom, which castrated the Kindred of Sub-Saharan Africa, as well as missing the opportunity to explore the rich mythological traditions on one-sixth of humanity. While people may complain about the KotE, they got their own unique supernatural creature and thirteen books (plus an important role in the metaplot). What did Africa get other than one book of weak tea?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T22:13:16-07:00","id":1069870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1067650-world-of-darkness-b-team?p=1069832#post1069832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regardless, I doubt that anyone are going to use the Romani, so their book can be ignored because it only effects 0.1% of humanity. The much more insulting book was Kindred of the Ebony Kingdom, which castrated the Kindred of Sub-Saharan Africa, as well as missing the opportunity to explore the rich mythological traditions on one-sixth of humanity. While people may complain about the KotE, they got their own unique supernatural creature and thirteen books (plus an important role in the metaplot). What did Africa get other than one book of weak tea?</div> </div> </div> </div>What's wrong with the Kindred of Sub-Saharan Africa? (I don't actually know. I've never even heard of that book)<br /> <br /> For that matter, what's a good source for info regarding the mythos and monsters of Sub-Saharan Africa?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T22:41:08-07:00","id":1069888,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't be too sure about the relative populations and what people play. I've seen a lot of Jewish characters (though mostly in Mage) despite Jews being (probably) the same sized population as Romani.<br /> <br /> I don't particularly feel like getting into the KotEK debates again, but while it has its problems, I find them considerably less problematic than KotE.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T08:28:41-07:00","id":1070100,"title":"","content":"Well, I do not have any problems with KotE and thought that WW did a tolerable job with the KJ. When it comes to KotEK, you have several problems. First, you had the same Clans with different hats syndrome, which was insulting when they had the example of KotE to show that they could make unique types of vampires for each continent. Second, you had two linked morality traits, Aye and Orun, where the combination of the two could not exceed 10 for most characters (Aye served as Humanity while Orun served as a dice pool cap for Disciplines). Third, you were automatically given fourteenth generation, with the lame excuse that all African Kindred were weaker than Kindred everywhere else because of excessive Embracing.<br /> <br /> So, you could have two Kindred, both Followers of Set, one of which was Embraced in Kassala, Sudan and one Embraced in Teseney, Eritrea. Despite being separated by only twenty miles, the Kindred Embraced in Sudan automatically lowers their generation by one and does not have the dice cap from Orun. That is why KotEK was not a good book (plus the treatment of African culture was rather poor).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T08:36:53-07:00","id":1070110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacecat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1067650-world-of-darkness-b-team?p=1069521#post1069521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just to clarify, my main concern is not so much to exclude certain groups because of their level of power but to exclude crowd favorites so that players will choose from among the more rarely used and the least used creature types.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, my apologies! I totally misunderstood what you were going for!<br /> <br /> Hm, this gets tricky. Crowd favorites and rarely used types is going to vary greatly from one player group to the next. It also gets messy since some stuff in some game line are difficult to define as core and non-core. Some even have various degrees of it. It'll also be hard to get a comprehensive list of books since a lot of this information is spread across a ton of places. I'll just stick to the major sources of info to help you get started in the right direction for the stuff that interests you, but understand that for most of these, there's a lot more out there. The focus here will be on things meant to be player characters. I'm not even going to get into things like Black Spiral Dancers or Marauders. Since popularity is so subjective, I won't comment on that.<br /> <br /> <b>Vampire: The Masquerade</b><br /> The most core you can get for this game are the major clans and the Camarilla and Sabbat divide. Past that on the clans side, you have the independent clans and a bunch of bloodlines. There are also other sects such the Anarchs, the Black Hand, and the Inconnu. <br /> Books: V20, Guide to the Camarilla, Guide to the Sabbat, Guide to the Anarchs, Anarchs Unbound, the clanbooks, Lore of the Clans, Lore of the Bloodlines, The Black Hand: A Guide to the Tal\u2019Mahe\u2019Ra<br /> <br /> Moving further afield, Kindred of the Ebony Kingdom describes the vampires of Africa. I've never read this one, but my understanding is that they're pretty similar to other Cainites.<br /> <br /> Kindred of the East describes Asian vampires. These guys are really their own supernatural creature with no ties at all to core book vampires.<br /> <br /> <b>Werewolf: The Apocalypse</b><br /> Werewolf is a pretty tightly focused game. The spot light is definitely on the Garou. For these guys, you've got W20, the tribebooks, and Players Guide to the Garou.<br /> <br /> The game does branch out into the various changing breeds, known collectively as the Fera. For info on them, look to W20, the breedbooks, Players Guide to the Changing Breeds, and W20 Changing Breeds.<br /> <br /> Hengeyokai details the Asian shifters, though they're really just the same Garou and Fera with a different culture.<br /> <br /> <b>Mage: The Ascension</b><br /> The main focus of Mage is the Tradition mages. Look to M20, the traditionbooks, and Guide to the Traditions for these guys.<br /> <br /> Later into Mage's run, the Technocracy mages became much more playable. M20, the conventionbooks, and Guide to the Technocracy have you covered here.<br /> <br /> The disparates are the collective term for the magical orders that don't fall under the Traditions or the Technocracy. Information about them is spread all over the place, but M20 collects them all together.<br /> <br /> Dragons of the East details Asian mages. I haven't read it, so this is about as much as I can say about it.<br /> <br /> <b>Wraith: The Oblivion</b><br /> Wraith focuses on the Stygian ghosts and their political factions \u2014 the hierarchy, heretics, renegades, and the guilds. You can find information about them in The Hierarchy, Renegades, the various guildbooks, and the forthcoming Wraith 20th.<br /> <br /> Outside of Stygia are the various other dark kingdoms whose ghosts work differently. To my knowledge, the only one to be published was the Dark Kingdom of Jade, which covered Asian ghosts. I think some of the other dark kingdoms will be covered in Wraith 20th, but I'm not sure.<br /> <br /> The Ferrymen are a special, mysterious faction of ghosts. They're covered in Ends of Empire.<br /> <br /> The Risen are ghosts who've reclaimed their bodies to finish some kind of unfinished business. Think The Crow. They're covered in The Risen.<br /> <br /> <b>Changeling: The Dreaming</b><br /> Changeling focuses on the Kithain and their Seelie and Unseelie courts. The Kithain include the major kiths plus a bunch of other kiths spread out between the various sourcebooks. C20, the kithbooks, and the three books of houses cover these guys.<br /> <br /> The Gallain are the different kinds of changelings that, to various degrees, don't work the same way as the Kithain. These include the Nunnehi (Native American fae), Menehune (Hawaiian fae), Inanimae (nature and elemental fae), Hsien (Asian fae), and the Adhene (fae that sided against the Kithain in a decisive war). Nunnehi are covered in the Players Guide. Menehune can be found in Shadows on the Hill. Inanimae are in Inanimae: The Secret Way. Hsien are covered by Land of Eight Million Dreams. Adhene were introduced in Denizens of the Dreaming. C20 has all of these guys.<br /> <br /> <b>Hunter: The Reckoning</b><br /> Hunter doesn't have any types that fall outside of the creeds. There are two creeds that are considered failed experiments by the Messengers, but they work mostly the same as any of the other creeds. You'll want Hunter: The Reckoning, the creedbooks, and the Hunter Players Guide.<br /> <br /> Hunter Holy War covers Middle Eastern Imbued. I haven't read it, but as I understand, it's the same creeds as the core book. Also, I remember it got a good bit of flack for being unintentionally racist back when it was released.<br /> <br /> <b>Demon: The Fallen</b><br /> Just like Hunter, Demon doesn't cover any demon types that fall outside the umbrella of the Fallen. Demon: The Fallen, Demon Players Guide, and Houses of the Fallen cover the main things.<br /> <br /> <b>Orpheus</b><br /> Orpheus focuses on living mortals who use technology to temporarily project their souls to the lands of the dead. It also has an alternate take on ghosts. Information about them is spread around the entire limited six book run.<br /> <br /> <b>World of Darkness</b><br /> The only supernatural type that doesn't belong to any game line are the Mummies. They started as a Vampire sourcebook, but got moved to a black cover World of Darkness book for their second edition, called World of Darkness: Mummy. They got reworked drastically for their third edition, called Mummy: The Resurrection. I think most folks consider the two entirely different supernatural creatures, although they're in the same continuity. The Mummy Players Guide details non-Egyptian mummies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T09:28:18-07:00","id":1070150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1067650-world-of-darkness-b-team?p=1070110#post1070110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hunter Holy War covers Middle Eastern Imbued. I haven't read it, but as I understand, it's the same creeds as the core book. Also, I remember it got a good bit of flack for being unintentionally racist back when it was released.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the first time I've heard this. Ever. From the old forums, to game tables in real life, etc.<br /> <br /> And after multiple readings, I'd have to disagree. <br /> <br /> The book was written by two Muslim men, of Middle-Eastern descent, who have always seemed to tackle religion and racism in a very progressive manner. Just goes to show you can't please everyone(not saying this about you, Pooka, just in general). The book goes into detail about common Western misconceptions of Islamic culture, offers numerous ways to expand ones knowledge of Islamic and Middle Eastern culture, and generally does a great job dispelling stereotypes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T09:50:54-07:00","id":1070165,"title":"","content":"I haven't read the book. I have no opinion on it of my own. I was just providing a heads up because I do remember there being come controversy over it back in the day on the original White Wolf forums.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T10:14:12-07:00","id":1070179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1067650-world-of-darkness-b-team?p=1070110#post1070110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah, my apologies! I totally misunderstood what you were going for!<br /> <br /> Hm, this gets tricky. Crowd favorites and rarely used types is going to vary greatly from one player group to the next. It also gets messy since some stuff in some game line are difficult to define as core and non-core. Some even have various degrees of it. It'll also be hard to get a comprehensive list of books since a lot of this information is spread across a ton of places. I'll just stick to the major sources of info to help you get started in the right direction for the stuff that interests you, but understand that for most of these, there's a lot more out there. The focus here will be on things meant to be player characters. I'm not even going to get into things like Black Spiral Dancers or Marauders. Since popularity is so subjective, I won't comment on that.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yup, the concept in itself is a bit of a mess, but you've helped greatly even before this post. So many books I've never even heard of!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T13:30:50-07:00","id":1070263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1067650-world-of-darkness-b-team?p=1069693#post1069693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, a specific book dedicated to a specific ethnic origin and any hypothetical interactions with various monsters in the WoD would still be intensely weird. There are probably other books - splats, location books, etc. - that could provide a better place with a tighter thesis for why it's there.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a valid argument. In all honesty, the only real reason to even consider a &quot;WoD: Gypsies/Romani&quot; book is the ethnic groups' historical place as a genre trope in Gothic Horror. And I'm not even entirely sold on it from that perspective. The only reason the book even still crosses my mind after all these years is, to quote Adam Pacitti, &quot;I can do it better, because I'm a smart ass.&quot; I perfect hindsight, you'd do better, I think, having a V:tM book on Nomads that would discuss them and Travelers in the same way it discussed Deadheads, truck drivers, wave chasing night surfers, carnies, and the like, one of more M:tAs books on &quot;ancient magic&quot; that covered them along side Jewish mystical traditions, Ancient Egypt, South Africa, Mayans and whatnot, the W:tO book on Mediums, and some stuff scattered in Kinfolk and the Silent Striders, Shadow Lords and Uktena tribebooks. And maybe the vampire hunting group as a small faction in Hunters Hunted who mostly operate in Eastern Europe. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T14:14:47-07:00","id":1070292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1067650-world-of-darkness-b-team?p=1069832#post1069832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While people may complain about the KotE, they got their own unique supernatural creature and thirteen books (plus an important role in the metaplot). What did Africa get other than one book of weak tea?</div> </div> </div> </div>Part of this is a matter of economics. For better or for worse, nerd culture has always been far more interested in East Asia than in Africa (or South Asia, or Latin America, or ...). That said, while I wish Africa had gotten more coverage*, the place is such a blank spot in the knowledge base of so many people - even more so 20 years ago - that it was likely never going to get more than a shallow and generalized coverage. Which is a shame, really. The place is so huge and diverse that the vampires of Liberia, Cape Town and Ethiopia should be as different from each other as those of Liverpool, Moscow and Sicily. Not necessarily different species - I was never hugely enamored with the Kuei-jin, mostly as I kept finding too many places in Asian cultures that the Kindred Clans seems to fit so well in - but as having strikingly different outlooks on unlife. There's a lot of potential for interesting stories about the vampire condition and just what it means to be one. <br /> <br /> <br /> *A Rage Across South Africa book looking at the country right after the end of apartheid and the uneasy relations between white Garou and black Fera, including the odd position Indian and Asian shifters in the area are in, would have, IMO at least, been really cool. Not to say it would've been done well, but, the idea is appealing.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T02:25:28-07:00","id":1071134,"title":"","content":"I'm baffled by why militant superhuman shapeshifters fighting a losing apocalyptic battle against the end of all things would pause to consider the racial politics of an irrelevant, artificial human state. <br /> <br /> <br /> The whole Legacies business of Kindred of the Ebony Kingdom was pretty awful to begin with; why give everything a new arbitrary name? Just call a spade a spade. It's not like the Vampires over the rest of the world would automatically use some standardized terminology; the clan names I mostly take as OOC terms which may have been formalized by the Camarilla, but which would have been antedated by a bevy of lingually/culturally specific names. Most of the stress on societal differences seemed to rely on the assumption that Western Kindred hew exclusively to stereotypes other books urge you to discount, a contradiction infuriatingly typical of White Wolf.<br /> <br /> <br /> In the settings my group has worked out, the phenomenon leading to the formation of Kue Jin is a universal rather than ethnically specific process; there's no such concept as distinct Underworld kingdoms nor any Hierarchy at all, with most of the (comparatively few, as Willpower 5 is extremely rare in our games) Wraiths dwell in the Shadowlands and Stygia is a desolate and enigmatic city of alien (Fallen) origin floating in the Tempest used by some Wraiths as a refuge; the 'Thousand Hells' concepts of the Kue Jin are generalized to the Onceborn and the Labyrinthe. Vampire vs. Kue Jin dynamics are dictated largely by stochastic propagation of Vampires from their origin in ancient mesopotamia; Europe, the Near East, and most of India are largely Cainite, as the initial proliferation of low generation Cainites capable of rapidly reproducing and suborning mortals (via ghouling) outcompeted the naturally arising Kue Jin type populations in early societies; displacement of established structures of such creatures early in the historical time of a society prevents the emergence of both organized cultivation of Dharma and reliable mechanisms of rescuing Chih Mei; as a result, while Kue Jin continue to stochastically arise in the West, their attrition rate is extremely high and they have little support network in most regions. Regions that posed larger geographic/temporal barriers to vampire spread, like the Far East, Sub Saharan Africa, and especially the Americas would have had enough people concentrating and dying before the arrival of Vampires to have robust Kue Jin creature societiies able to resist sporadic cainite incursion; hence, the limited penetration of Cainites into both regions, where Kue Jin type half wraiths continue to predominate (the devastation of Native AMerican societies by plague and the systematic marginalization of the survivors fatally destabilized extant Mesoamerican supernatural social structures, enabling for the rise to predominance of Cainites there). Thus, the whole arbitrary and nonsensical 'eastern vamp' vs. 'western vamp' divide becomes a competition between a rapidly proliferating strain of supernatural of specific origin vs. a 'natural' and universal phenomenon that occurs at a frequency proportionate to death rate (tuned by historical trends more likely to produce the sort of sinner that might find themselves subject to the Kue Jin ordeal. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10809-andkat","name":"Andkat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T02:55:58-07:00","id":1071151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Andkat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1067650-world-of-darkness-b-team?p=1071134#post1071134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm baffled by why militant superhuman shapeshifters fighting a losing apocalyptic battle against the end of all things would pause to consider the racial politics of an irrelevant, artificial human state.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because it's essential to the nature of their enemy.<br /> <br /> Racism (and bigotry in general) makes the Wyrm stronger. While the Garou suck at healing the wounds in human societies, any successes they make in that arena is a positive impact on the larger war. That's why there's multiple Tribes that concern themselves with human politics as a regular part of their core philosophy; from the idealistic Children of Gaia that see it as a moral good anyway, to the extremely pragmatic Shadow Lords who only care if it achieves their overarching goals.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The whole Legacies business of Kindred of the Ebony Kingdom was pretty awful to begin with; why give everything a new arbitrary name? </div> </div> </div>Because:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> the clan names I mostly take as OOC terms... </div> </div> </div>This is explicitly incorrect. The Clan names, while not static over the course of history, and definitely noted as having more variety in the past before the Camarilla and Sabbat spread a unified jargon, are not OOC terms. They're IC terms.<br /> <br /> There's also the sheer aesthetic matter of giving the &quot;local&quot; names for the Clans in a given area (Veil of Night did it for Dark Ages Middle Eastern vampires) for what African vampires would actually call themselves to each other. And, of course, some of the Legacies are called the same thing as their non-African counterparts, and there are some minor differences that would at least qualify a few of the Legacies to be Clan variants/Bloodlines (which the books given unique names to anyway).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T05:20:11-07:00","id":1071194,"title":"","content":"I am not quite sure why Willpower 5 would be rare. I cannot think of a single game of cWoD that I have played in the past twenty years or so where there was a PC with Willpower below 5 (I personally have never played a character with a Willpower below 8). In WtA and WtO, Willpower 5+ makes up a quarter of the mortal population, and Willpower 10 is not that rare at 0.5% of the mortal population.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I agree that KJ should be considered the 'native' vampires of every culture while Kindred should always be considered the 'invading' vampires. The vampirism of the Kindred is the ultimate intimate communicable disease because it preserves the existence of its carriers potentially forever. Even if you manage to annihilate every active Kindred across the globe, there could be thousands of Kindred in torpor that could restart the infection centuries after you stop guarding against it. The vampirism of the KJ is intensely personal, like a cancer, and cannot be transmitted through a crass exchange of fluids like the vampirism of the Kindred.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T16:16:10-07:00","id":1071479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Andkat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1067650-world-of-darkness-b-team?p=1071134#post1071134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm baffled by why militant superhuman shapeshifters fighting a losing apocalyptic battle against the end of all things would pause to consider the racial politics of an irrelevant, artificial human state.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because a majority of them are born and raised as human beings and many never manage to completely get over the problems of &quot;monkey-think&quot; (as one of the Silent Strider Revised narrators referred to it). On top of this, they have strong cultural and emotional ties to their Kinfolk groups, often being (over)protective of them and their perceived interests. If you are, for example, a 1994-era Get of Fenris from South Africa's Dutch-descended Afrikaner ethnic group, then even as you are battling the forces of the Wyrm in the Transvaal, you probably have serious concerns about your Kinfolk family and the possibility of some sort of forthcoming ethnic cleansing (such as what happened in neighboring Zimbabwe). And to make matters more complicated, said Get of Fenris may actually end up having more in common with a Zulu-born Simba or San-born Mokole than she would with some soutpiel Fianna or Silver Fang who grew up on the Cape. I, personally, find this sort of potential character motivation and interaction endlessly fascinating. <br /> <br /> That's the in-character motivation. The out-of-character game line motivation would be that RPGs can be a useful tool to explore real world issues through fictional stand ins. Werewolf especially liked to deal with real world socially progressive and environmental causes. The long running and often violent animosity between the Garou, who are primarily Euro-Asian in origin, and the Fera, a number of whom are linked to Africa, offered a lens for examining issues of race relations, especially in a region as much in the news as South Africa was in the 1990s. Which, again, I would've found interesting. Even if in hindsight I don't think White Wolf could've done it all that well back in the day. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T18:36:10-07:00","id":1071527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is explicitly incorrect. The Clan names, while not static over the course of history, and definitely noted as having more variety in the past before the Camarilla and Sabbat spread a unified jargon, are not OOC terms. They're IC terms. </div> </div> </div>Yeah except that this is another blatantly inane part of how WW has written the setting and accepting it is to throw all verisimilitude out the window; why would a few terms particular to Castilian Spanish be near-universal descriptors for three of the major clans, several of which (Brujah, Toreador) aren't even principally concentrated in that part of the world? Most Ancillae and Elders of the Dark Ages would remember a time when Christian Spain comprised nothing more than a northern rump state in an Iberian peninsula dominated by an Arabic-speaking aristocracy...and plenty more Elders and Methuselaths times long before that. Realistically, any 'universal' nomenclature for the clans would consist of time-worn and somewhat mutilated Sumerian, Akkadian, Phoenician, or Aramaic terms practiced by some Elders, scholars, and the particularly pretentious; otherwise whether Western, Near Eastern, Indian, or African, Kindred nomenclature should vary with the age of the local social milieu/given subs-strata present (the Elders in a given locale and their closely held childer probably use quite different vocabulary- and language outright- than the neonates) at a gathering and the nature of the local vernacular or widely accepted diplomatic tongue. You might accept that centuries after the formation of the Camarilla the Camarilla would try to apply some semi-standard jargon, but that's about it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10809,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10809-andkat","user":"Andkat","date":". 03-31-2017, 09:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10809-andkat","name":"Andkat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T18:52:31-07:00","id":1071538,"title":"","content":"I'm not defending the quality of the names in the game as written.<br /> <br /> The issue was you essentially trying to claim the Legacies represent an inherently problematic setting element because they don't jive with how you want the Clan names to work, rather than how they actually work (however stupid how they actually work is).<br /> <br /> It doesn't matter that the Clan names are nonsensical based on real world knowledge of languages and naming. It doesn't matter that European Kindred somehow managed to standardize a set of terms far too effectively (and without resorting to a specific language) for the time, and then the main Sects that arose out of that period spread that terminology to a near global status.<br /> <br /> It matters that despite however you want to explain it, that's still what the games say happened.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-01T08:10:07-07:00","id":1071715,"title":"","content":"I always interpret the Clan names as being modern inventions that spread during the Enlightenment. Among the Elders and Methuselahs, I have them using other names (Taurakathapsian, 'bull dancer' or 'bull leaper' being one of the Elder names for the Toreader Clan, in reference to their Antediluvian's dominion over the Bull of Heaven). I think that the majority of Elders and Methuselahs refrain from using the vulgar terms of the Enlightenment as names for the Clans. This is also linguistically appropriate, as words like Brujah and Toreador are modern words that would not have existed in the 13th century.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-01T13:00:53-07:00","id":1071795,"title":"","content":"Again, however nonsensical the names might be, the games state that at least in Europe, the Clan names were essentially codified by the 12th Century. There's no real room for &quot;interpretation&quot; here. We have source books that cover vampire life in the 1100s and Europe is depicted as having Clan names that have come into common use across Europe already; with zero mention of older vampires using older terms for the vast majority of Clans.<br /> <br /> Again, not saying this is a good thing, but altering it from this is a matter of house rules, not interpretation, and thus shouldn't be the basis for judging things like the naming of Legacies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}